# AtomicDB sweep of stale backed values (sweep_stale_backed), example unit.
#
# Copy this and its .timer to /etc/systemd/system/, then:
#
#     sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#     sudo systemctl enable --now atomicdb-backed-sweep.timer
#     journalctl -u atomicdb-backed-sweep.service -f
#
# WHAT A RUN DOES.  It carries on the ascents that a guard cut since the last
# run (their frontier is in the BACKED_GUARD event), checks the positions
# where overlapping ingests met, and reads a slice of the table sized so that
# all of it is read every seven days.  What one level of the backup would
# rewrite is checked again five minutes later; only what is still stale, with
# the same stored numbers and no ingest of its own pending, is repaired, by
# the ordinary ascent, in short transactions, never on a proven position.  The
# receipt is a BACKED_SWEEP event.  The docstring of
# atomicdb/management/commands/sweep_stale_backed.py has the reasons and the
# measurements.
#
# WHY NOT atomicdb-recascade.  That one recomputes every position with edges
# in one pass, and at 75 million positions a pass stopped fitting in a night
# (stopped since 5-Oct-2026, see its drop-in).  This one checks a slice per
# run and writes only what is stale: about 12 seconds of checks per run at
# the size of 26-Oct-2026, then the five minutes of settling, then repairs.
#
# BOUNDS.  The command's own: --max-seconds 600 and --max-changes 10000 per
# run.  TimeoutStartSec below is the hard stop.  One run at a time: the timer
# never starts a oneshot that is still running, and the command takes a
# PostgreSQL advisory lock against a second copy started by hand.  It loses
# against everything with someone waiting: low CPU and I/O weight, and a
# lock_timeout of 0.2 s on any row an ingest holds, below the 1 s
# deadlock_timeout, so a deadlock check never picks an ingest for it.

[Unit]
Description=AtomicDB sweep of stale backed values
Documentation=https://github.com/Belzedar94/OpenBench
After=network-online.target postgresql.service
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=root
WorkingDirectory=/opt/openbench
EnvironmentFile=/etc/openbench/atomicdb-pg.env
Environment=OPENBENCH_DEBUG=False
Environment=PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
ExecStartPre=/bin/bash -c "systemctl set-environment OPENBENCH_SECRET_KEY=$(cat /opt/openbench/Config/secret.key)"
ExecStart=/opt/openbench/.venv/bin/python -u manage.py sweep_stale_backed
TimeoutStartSec=1200
Nice=15
IOSchedulingClass=idle
CPUWeight=10
IOWeight=10
MemoryMax=2G
